          P("The word for *you* (one person) is **ikáw**. It becomes **ka** when it comes after the main word (Lessons 5 and 6 explain this). When greeting an elder or a superior, Tagalogs use the plurals **kayó** (*you*) and **silá** (*they*) instead of ka. Pô may be dropped if kayó or silá is used."),
